Module gaunt "A Winter in Carth" {
  // ── Dame Hawise Strake, the Lady Penitentiary ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  // Born in the Row, a proxy at twelve beside Hern; rose by being better at it than anyone. Warm, worldly, funny,
  // partial, a politician; she bends small rules for the Row every day and is proud of it. She believes, with reason,
  // that the Commerce feeds the Row in winter: "I have turned vanity into bread." Her exactness is about one thing: the
  // sentence. She will put out the man she loved, fairly. By day at her desk she is the Penitentiary; on Fastens' Eve,
  // masked, she ladles soup at the Barefoot copper in the Row, as she has for thirty years, and is no one.
  Person hawise "Dame Hawise Strake" at penitentiary {
    Role "the Lady Penitentiary, a broad handsome woman of sixty in grey, with a pen behind her ear and the Row still in her voice" when not masked(hawise).
    Role "a masked woman in a grey shawl ladling soup at the Barefoot copper, with a voice from the Row" when masked(hawise).
    Ancestry human. Peaceable. Pronouns she. Manner cheerful.
    Greets "The woman at the desk by the fire looks up, and takes the pen from behind her ear, and points it at the chair. 'Sit. You're the stranger who brought Ninian in, or the one who didn't. Either way you've walked with him, so you'll have opinions. Everybody who walks with Ninian comes away with opinions.' She smiles, and it is a wonderful smile. 'Mine are on the wall.' The forty books of the Register stand behind her on their lecterns.".
    Greets again "Dame Hawise looks up from the Register and smiles.".
  }
  Relation masked(group). Measure hawiseReasons(group). Query hawiseMoved() means hawiseReasons(hawise) >= 2.
  Relation hawiseHeardCarth(group). Relation hawiseHeardHern(group). Relation hawiseHeardVerse(group).
  Relation carryingHern(group). Relation carryingHawise(group). Relation hernHeardHawise(group).
  Relation ringGiven(group). Relation metMasked(group).
  // Her days: the Penitentiary from eight to five; Fastens' Eve, masked, at the Barefoot copper from nine to eleven;
  // Ash Day, the Chapter House.
  Rule hawise_desk when daytime() and not masked(hawise) and not at(hawise, penitentiary) and not sitting() and not afterTrial(hawise) { Assert at(hawise, penitentiary). }
  Rule hawise_home when not daytime() and at(hawise, penitentiary) and not masked(hawise) { Assert at(hawise, limbo). }
  Rule hawise_masks when eveDay() and hour(clock) >= 21 and hour(clock) < 23 and not masked(hawise) and not spread(hawise_masked_done) { Assert masked(hawise). Assert at(hawise, limbo). }
  Rule hawise_unmasks when masked(hawise) and (hour(clock) >= 23 or not eveDay()) { Retract masked(hawise). Assert at(hawise, limbo). Assert spread(hawise_masked_done). }
  Entity hawise_masked_done: fact "the Lady at the copper".
  Relation afterTrial(group).
  // Under the mask she is nobody: written as a person of her own, there only while the mask is on, so that nobody in
  // the Row (and nothing on the page) calls her by her name.
  Person masked "the masked woman at the copper" at limbo {
    Role "a broad woman in a grey shawl and a black half-mask, ladling soup, with a voice from the Row". Ancestry human. Peaceable. Pronouns she. Manner cheerful.
    Greets "The masked woman holds out a bowl to you without looking, then looks. 'You're not Row,' she says. 'Have some anyway. It's Fastens' Eve.'".
    Seen when masked(hawise).
  }
  Rule mask_on when masked(hawise) and not at(masked, row_lane) { Assert at(masked, row_lane). }
  Rule mask_off when not masked(hawise) and at(masked, row_lane) { Assert at(masked, limbo). }
  Observe copper_masked at row_lane when masked(hawise) "At the Barefoot copper by the Hall door a masked woman in a grey shawl is ladling soup into the bowls held out to her, a ladle a bowl, never spilling, talking to everyone in the queue by name, and the queue talking back. Some of them call her Duchess. Nobody calls her anything else.".

  // ── At her desk ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Topic hawise_commerce with hawise "Ask the Lady Penitentiary whether the Commerce of Merit does anyone any good" when not masked(hawise) once {
    Says "'Good!' She laughs. 'It feeds the Row through the winter. Do you know what the Row was before the Commerce? I do. I was in it. A burgess has a sin on his conscience; before, he'd buy a candle and forget it. Now he buys a fast, and a woman in the Row eats for a week.' She taps the nearest book. 'Vanity, into bread. I've done that every day for thirty years. Ninian says nobody's sorry. He's right. Nobody's fed by sorrow either.' She puts the pen back behind her ear. 'He was always better at being right than at being useful. I was always the other.'".
  }
  Topic hawise_hern with hawise "Ask the Lady Penitentiary what will happen to Ninian Hern" when not masked(hawise) once {
    Says "Her face does not change at all, which is how you know. 'He'll be heard,' she says. 'Ash Day, noon, the Chapter House. Canon Pellow will prosecute, gently; the Faculty will determine, expensively; and I will ask him whether he recants. If he does, he goes home to the Row and does three years' penance by proxy, which the Barefoot will do for him for nothing, and that's the end of it.' She dips her pen. 'If he doesn't, I will put him out at the Gate of Ash at dusk, in what he stands in.' She writes a line. 'He never had a coat worth the name. I've had one made. It's in that cupboard. Don't tell him.'".
  }
  Topic hawise_law with hawise "Ask the Lady Penitentiary whether a sentence of putting-out may be borne by another" when not masked(hawise) once {
    Says "She puts down her pen. 'Who's been reading the canons to you?' She looks at you, hard, for the first time. 'Yes. It's a penance; the greatest. Any penance may be borne. It's never been tried. A Lady Penitentiary who had it offered in the Chapter House would have to decide whether the law means what it says.' She picks up the pen again. 'I'd sooner not be that Lady Penitentiary,' she says, lightly. 'But I would decide.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, sentence_borne). }
  }
  Topic hawise_pellow with hawise "Tell the Lady Penitentiary what Canon Pellow's men do on the north tower at night" when knows(actor, unbuilding) and not pellowExposed(pellow) and not pellowBargain(pellow) once {
    Says "Dame Hawise listens without a word, writing nothing. When you have done she sits back. 'The frost,' she says. 'Fifty-three years of frost.' Then she laughs, quite helplessly, with her hand over her eyes. 'Oh, Hamo. Oh, the Fabric.' She stops laughing. 'He'll not prosecute anybody on Ash Day for saying the Commerce is a fraud. Not in my Chapter House. I'll have the precentor do it, who believes in nothing and reads beautifully.' She makes a note. 'Thank you. I've wondered about that tower since I was twelve.'".
    On discuss { Assert pellowExposed(pellow). Increase hawiseReasons(hawise) by 1. }
  }
  Topic hawise_ladder with hawise "Tell the Lady Penitentiary that Mistress Dinsdale and Master Sowerby are buying penance in advance to race each other up the Ladder" when knows(actor, dinsdale_hiring) and not ladderExposed(dinsdale) and not masked(hawise) once {
    Says "'In advance.' Dame Hawise closes her eyes. 'For faults they haven't done.' She opens them. 'That's not penance, that's a subscription.' She writes. 'Both of them down a rung on Ash Day, and the advances forfeit to the Barefoot Hall.' She looks up. 'Don't look so pleased. They'll be back up next year. People always are. That's what the Ladder's for.'".
    On discuss { Assert ladderExposed(dinsdale). }
  }

  // ── Under the mask ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Topic masked_who with masked "Ask the masked woman at the copper who she is" when masked(hawise) and not metMasked(actor) once {
    Says "'Nobody,' says the masked woman. 'It's Fastens' Eve. Nobody's anybody.' She ladles. 'I came out of this Row at twelve. Fasted for a fishmonger's wife with a boy who ate her cat's dinner on the fourth day and made me eat half. Every Fastens' Eve since I've come down and ladled, because on Fastens' Eve you can.' She looks at you through the eyeholes. 'You've walked with Ninian Hern,' she says. 'It's all over you. Opinions.' The ladle stops. 'Go on, then. It's Fastens' Eve. Say what you like to nobody.'".
    On discuss { Assert metMasked(actor). }
  }
  Topic masked_carth with masked "Tell the masked woman about the night at Carth" when masked(hawise) and metMasked(actor) and stayingAtCarth(actor) and not hawiseHeardCarth(hawise) once {
    Says "You tell her: the dark, the hearth, the hand in the ash; the child's cough, the old man in the byre, the old woman lying down with him. She goes on ladling the whole time, a ladle a bowl, never spilling. When you get to the old woman, she misses a bowl. The man holding it says nothing; he waits. She fills it. 'Forty nights,' she says. 'I set it. It's the penance for blood. I set it on a farm.' The next bowl. 'I've never seen a vigil kept. In thirty years. I've the Register. I've Raistrick's sticks.' She ladles. 'Go on,' she says. 'The old woman. Go on.'".
    On discuss { Assert hawiseHeardCarth(hawise). Increase hawiseReasons(hawise) by 1. }
  }
  Topic masked_hern_word with masked "Give the masked woman Hern's word: the soup was always too salt" when masked(hawise) and metMasked(actor) and carryingHern(actor) and not hawiseHeardHern(hawise) once {
    Says "The ladle stops. The masked woman stands quite still with it held over the copper, dripping, and the queue waits, and nobody says anything, because it is the Row. Then she puts the ladle down and lifts her mask a little, just to wipe her eyes, and puts it back. 'We made it,' she says. 'When we were fifteen. The Hall's first soup. I salted it, and he said it was too salt, and I said he could fast, then. Forty-five years.' She picks up the ladle. 'It's still too salt,' she says. 'I've never changed it. Tell him—' She stops. 'No. I'll tell him.'".
    On discuss { Assert hawiseHeardHern(hawise). Increase hawiseReasons(hawise) by 1. }
  }
  Topic masked_verse with masked "Sing the masked woman the end of the children's sliding rhyme" when masked(hawise) and metMasked(actor) and knows(actor, second_verse) and not hawiseHeardVerse(hawise) once {
    Says "You sing it, badly, the end the Row's children sing on the ditch: at the top he set him down: NOW WALK, said Oswy, into town. The masked woman laughs out loud. 'We sang that,' she says. 'Ninian and me, on the ditch, when it froze. I'd forgotten there was an end to it. It's not on the plinth.' She ladles. 'Now walk.' She stops. 'He carried him up, and set him down, and said, now walk. Not, I've done it for you. Now walk.' She looks up at the Close wall, over the Row, where the Penitentiary's forty windows are dark. 'I've been carrying the whole city for thirty years,' she says, 'and never once set it down.'".
    On discuss { Assert hawiseHeardVerse(hawise). Increase hawiseReasons(hawise) by 1. }
  }
  Topic masked_save with masked "Ask the masked woman what would save Ninian Hern" when masked(hawise) and metMasked(actor) and hawiseReasons(hawise) >= 1 and not carryingHawise(actor) once {
    Says "'Nothing,' she says at once. 'He won't let it.' She ladles. Then, quietly: 'He could say he was sorry once. Not that he's wrong. Not that the Commerce is good. Just that once, in thirty years, for one of them, he was sorry: really sorry, his own sorrow, not bought. It would be true. I know it's true. I was there.' She fills a bowl. 'That's a recantation. In the canons, that's enough; the heresy is that nobody's sorry. One man sorry, once, and the proposition's false, and I can let him go home.' She does not look at you. 'He won't say it. He'll think it's giving in. Tell him it's giving me the words.'".
    On discuss { Assert carryingHawise(actor). }
  }
  Kind gaunt_ring "Dame Hawise's ring, a plain silver ring with the Penitentiary's billet of keys on it" is treasure worth 0 weighing 0.
  Item ring "Dame Hawise's ring" is gaunt_ring at limbo.
  Topic masked_ring with masked "Ask the masked woman for remission of your pains" when masked(hawise) and metMasked(actor) and hawiseMoved() and not ringGiven(hawise) once {
    Says "She laughs, and holds the ladle out to the next bowl, and while she fills it she works a ring off her finger with her thumb and drops it on the step beside the copper. 'Remission,' she says. 'Show that at the Close Gate. It's no good anywhere else in the world, but in Gaunt it's the Lady Penitentiary's ring, and you owe nothing.' She does not look at you. 'Nobody gave it to you. It's Fastens' Eve.'".
    On discuss { Assert ringGiven(hawise). Assert at(ring, row_lane). }
  }
  Action show_ring(actor: group, site: place) "Show the porter of the Close Gate the Lady Penitentiary's ring" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, close_gate_street) and carries(actor, ring) and not shriven() and tallied(actor).
    Time 1 minute.
    On success { Set pains(actor) to 0. Retract forgedTally(actor). }
    Result "The porter looks at the ring through the grille for a long moment. Then he takes your tally, and with his knife he shaves every notch off it, slowly, one by one, until it is a smooth white stick, and gives it back. 'Remitted,' he says. He does not ask how.".
  }
  // Moved, she does the one thing in her gift that is not the sentence: she sends her own physician to the gaol.
  Rule hawise_sends_physician when hawiseMoved() and hernFailing(hern) and hernGaoled(hern) and not hernTended(hern) and not hernDead(hern) { Assert hernTended(hern). }
  Relation hernTended(group).
}
